3.Difference between fetch and pull
Both commands get the latest changes from the remote repository
GitFetch: Get the latest changes but doesnot change current branch or working code
GitPull: Get the latest changes and immediatly integrates changes into current branch

4. Git commands:
Command	Purpose
git init	Creates a new Git repository
git clone	Copies a remote repository to your computer
git status	Shows the current status of your files
git add	Adds changes to the staging area
git commit	Saves staged changes to Git history
git push	Uploads commits to a remote repository
git pull	Downloads and integrates changes from a remote repository
git fetch	Downloads remote changes without integrating them
git branch	Creates or lists branches
git checkout	Switches branches or restores files
git switch	Switches between branches
git merge	Combines one branch with another
git log	Shows commit history
git diff	Shows changes between versions
git remote	Manages remote repositories
git reset	Undoes or moves changes/commits
git revert	Creates a new commit that undoes a previous commit
git rm	Removes a file from Git
git mv	Renames or moves a file

git bash:
It si an command line terminal for windows that comes with git.That allows you to integrate with the terminal.
